        <referenceFunction amount="1.0" category="fuels" datasetRelatesToProduct="true" generalComment="The data should be considered as an approximation, because they describe the operation of a UO2 fuel fabrication plant, for lack of specific information. Only radioactive emissions to air and water have been taken from the few data avalable on the Hanau plant (closed). The MOX fuel is made of plutonium from reprocessed spent fuel and depleted uranium from enrichment of fresh uranium. The environmental burdens from reprocessing are in this study entirely allocated to the spent fuel, the burdens from enrichment entirely allocated to the enriched uranium. Hence, the MOX fuel is neither directly charged of reprocessing nor of enrichment, but the fuel chain consistently takes into account the total emissions form these two steps.    ;&#10;UUID: 1105af2e-20e3-3297-b5f8-c9d854f6aec1" includedProcesses="The module uses the same data set of a UO2 fuel fabrication plant." infrastructureProcess="false" localCategory="fuels" localName="MOX fuel element for LWR, at nuclear fuel fabrication plant" localSubCategory="uranium\fuel element" name="MOX fuel element for LWR, at nuclear fuel fabrication plant" subCategory="uranium\fuel element" unit="kg"/>
